      "summaryMarkdown": "`release-plz.toml` matches RPZ-1 and RayX.CLI's template (only intended deltas: `git_release_enable = true`, `semver_check` off with the 1.x rationale, two `[[package]]` entries in version group `dtcg`, derive keeps the inherited `git_tag_name`, and the `commit.footers` Migration loop). Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock change only the four 0.1.0 -> 1.0.0 strings; nothing under `crates/` differs from `7d55b99`; the derive dev-dependency stays path-only. CHANGELOG.md diff is only the header and the heading. The recorded passing preview log shows the first-release dry run planning `v1.0.0` + git release and `no release method enabled` for the derive crate. An independent scratch run (temp copy, local stub forge) confirmed the template renders each `Migration:` footer (two footers tested) as a nested line under a scoped `feat` entry and keeps unscoped entries correct, with 1.1.0 proposed. Observation only: the header still states the crates follow SemVer although the 1.x policy ships breaks as minors; this is the owner's binding decision and RPZ-1's required header, so it is not a finding. Non-blocking recommendations (not defects): (1) the preview's docs-only scenario uses `git diff --quiet`, which ignores untracked files; `test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\"` would prove the clean tree fully. (2) release-plz dates generated sections in UTC (a scratch run at ~00:10 +02:00 on 2026-10-19 produced `## [1.1.0] - 2026-10-18` above `## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-19`); when t09 sets or corrects the 1.0.0 date, use the UTC date of the release push (`date -u +%F`).",
